%T A399831 4,9,2,4,4,8,2,8,2,6,6,4,2,8,3,6,4,6,2,8,4,8,4,4,2,12,2,4,6,7,4,8,2,6,
%U A399831 4,8,2,12,2,4,6,6,4,8,2,8,4,4,2,12,4,4,4,8,2,12
%N A399831 The number of divisors d of n such that gcud(d, n/d) is an exponentially odd number (A268335), where gcud is the greatest common unitary divisor.
%C A399831 First differs from A252505, A365173, A365680, A366991, and A390555 at n = 32, and from A399828 at n = 64.
%C A399831 The sum of these divisors is A399837(n).
%H A399831 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A399831/b399831.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A399831 Vaclav Kotesovec, <a href="/A399831/a399831.jpg">Graph - the asymptotic ratio (10000 terms)</a>
%F A399831 Multiplicative with a(p^e) = e if e is a multiple of 4, and e + 1 otherwise.
%F A399831 Dirichlet g.f.: zeta(s) * zeta(4*s) * Product_{p prime} (1 + 1/p^s + 1/p^(2*s) + 1/p^(3*s) - 1/p^(4*s) + 1/p^(5*s)).
%F A399831 From _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Sep 24 2026: (Start)
%F A399831 Let f(s) = Product_{p prime} 1 - (p^s - 1)/((p^s + 1)*(p^(2*s) + 1)*p^(2*s)).
%F A399831 Dirichlet g.f.: zeta(s)^2 * f(s).
%F A399831 Sum_{k=1..n} a(k) ~ f(1) * n * (log(n) + 2*gamma - 1 + f'(1)/f(1)), where
%F A399831 f(1) = Product_{p prime} 1 - (p - 1)/((p + 1)*(p^2 + 1)*p^2) = A393897 = 0.9764597623531743379601646228536240762385503022192694203739709649602...,
%F A399831 f'(1) = f(1) * Sum_{p prime} 2*(2*p^4-p^3-p^2-p-1) * log(p) / ((p^3+p^2+p+1)*(p^5+p^4+p^3+p^2-p+1)) = f(1) * 0.0544312341864715711355958510727299091323871314764971664711166455171...
%F A399831 and gamma is the Euler-Mascheroni constant A001620. (End)
%t A399831 f[p_, e_] := If[Mod[e, 4] == 0, e, e + 1]; a[1] = 1; a[n_] := Times @@ f @@@ FactorInteger[n]; Array[a, 100]
%o A399831 (PARI) a(n) = vecprod(apply(x -> if(x % 4 == 0, x, x+1), factor(n)[, 2]));
%Y A399831 Cf. A268335, A077610, A165430, A225174, A384244.
%Y A399831 Cf. A365173 (analogous with gcd), A399837.
%Y A399831 Cf. A252505, A365173, A365680, A366991, A390555.
%Y A399831 Cf. A393897.
%Y A399831 The number of divisors d of n such that gcud(d, n/d) is: A286324 (1), A399828 (squarefree), A399829 (powerful), A399830 (square), this sequence (exponentially odd), A399832 (odd), A399833 (power of 2).
